    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12059" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπηλῐ-ώτης</span></b>  (with or without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμος</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>east wind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.188
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.23
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζέφυρος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				363b13
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Mu.</u>
				394b23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Vent.</u>
				973a13
			</span></i>, al.—The 
				Ion.
			 form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπηλιώτης</span> is
			retained in 
				Att.
			, and appears on the Tower of Andronicus Cyrrhestes, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				518
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφηλιώτης</span> on a later
			table of the winds, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1308
			</span></i>, and in Latin authors, Catull.<i><span class="en">
				26.3
			</span></i>, Seneca<i><span class="en">
				<u>QN</u>
				5.16.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gell.
				2.22.8
			</span></i>.</div>
